## Why Tasks Cannot Be Parallelized

- Static/API verification should use the docs and evidence rules created in Phase 1.
- Fresh-user QA should not start until static checks pass, because device QA is slower and depends on a runnable API/mobile build.
- Failure and cross-user access tests should run after the happy path succeeds so failures can be interpreted clearly.
- Negative-path verification often uncovers fixes in shared server trust-boundary code and should be the final gate.

